 to require an ACL","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/t_WbSvcRqACL.md","line":46},{"title":"Add a path-based ACL for a scripted REST API","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/add-a-path-based-acl-for-a-scripted-rest-api.md","line":51},{"title":"Configure a scripted REST API resource to require an ACL","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/t_WbSvcOpRqACL.md","line":53},{"title":"View path-based ACLs from REST API Explorer","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/view-path-based-acls-from-rest-api-explorer.md","line":55},{"title":"Scripted REST APIs","target":"c_CustomWebServices","line":59},{"title":"Web services","target":"r_AvailableWebServices","line":60}],"metadata":{"title":"View path-based ACLs","description":"Path-based Access Control Levels \\(ACLs\\) enable you to define access control rules for scripted REST API endpoints using their resource path. This can be done independently of the ACL references on the operation record. Path-based ACLs enable more flexible security configurations, especially for read-only APIs and guest user experiences.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/view-path-based-acls.html","release":"australia","product":"REST API Explorer","classification":"rest-api-explorer","topic_type":"task","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":1,"breadcrumb":["Configure a scripted REST API to require an ACL","Create a scripted REST API","Scripted REST APIs","REST APIs","Web services","API implementation","API implementation and reference"],"tags":["#api-reference","#rest","#api-explorer","#testing","#endpoints","#type-task"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/api-reference/rest-api-explorer/view-path-based-acls.md"},
